    "objetivo": "Check what you can do at the end of level A2: say how long something has lasted with «da» and the present, answer a call, accept an invitation, make a polite request, tell a short story in the past and talk about plans. Use «non» with «mai» after the verb, «di» in «credo di sì», and «essere» in «sono arrivato». Avoid the English-speaker traps: «per» for a situation that goes on, «Questo è» on the phone and «ho» with a verb of movement.",
